  RESIDUAL, NOT FIXED BY THIS ITEM (reported, not absorbed — see the return report):
    Raising the recessed-plate floor from 0.42 to 0.62 lifts every colour inside a
    recessed plate, but not all of them past 4.5:1. Measured on the same ground:
      --gold-pale  at 0.62   5.62:1   PASS  (the mark this item was opened for)
      --mist-200   at 0.62   5.20:1   PASS  (was 2.98:1 at the 0.42 floor)
      --white      at 0.62   7.22:1   PASS  (was 3.86:1 at the 0.42 floor)
      --mist-400   at 0.62   2.98:1   FAIL  (was 1.98:1 at the 0.42 floor)
    So the vitrine's secondary text (--mist-400: .repo, .metric dt, .limitsLabel,
    .stamp, .notDeployed, .exclusion dd) is improved by 50% and still short of AA
    while its plate is recessed. Clearing it needs the plate floor at ~0.84, which
    erases the raking light the section is built on — i.e. it is a redesign of the
    dimming mechanism, not a token swap, and it is outside this item's smallest
    change. Recorded here and in the return report; not silently absorbed.
